Z||000000||87FieroGTx||06-07-2001||02:43 AM|||| Will a 3.4 V6 drop in a 87 GT or would I have to change mounts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||06-07-2001||04:14 AM||||it will fit right in -- just a few minor modifications need to be made but as for the mounts, they are all the same.......<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||06-07-2001||10:10 AM||||Here we go again.  Yeah, this is one of the more often asked questions.  A wealth of info is available on here about every different kind of 3.4 swap you can imagine.  Just do a search to find it.  Just remember, the swap depends on the type of 3.4 you're talking about.<P>3.4 pushrod RWD from F-body<BR>3.4 pushrod FWD from minivan<BR>3.4 DOHC from Grand Prix GTP/Lumina Z34<BR>3400SFI from 99+ Grand Am<P>The standard swap is the 3.4 RWD from an F-body.  It's almost a drop in and can be dressed with the Fiero accessories to look stock.  All the others require more work.  The 3400SFI may not be possible due to drastic changes in accessory and engine mounts.  Not to mention electronics.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||06-07-2001||12:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>The 3400SFI may not be possible due to drastic changes in accessory and engine mounts.  Not to mention electronics.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You said it buddy! The aluminum head 3.4's are a major PITA to swap.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
